1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,680
If milk or ice cream leaves you bloated, gassy, or running to the bathroom, you're not imagining it — that could be lactose intolerance.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:24,720
The NIH estimates that thirty to fifty million Americans deal with it, and it hits some groups far harder than others: up to ninety percent of Asian Americans and eighty percent of Black Americans have it, compared to as little as fifteen percent of people with Northern European ancestry.

3
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:31,280
It comes down to lactase, the enzyme your small intestine uses to break down lactose, the sugar in dairy.

4
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:41,360
When you're not making enough lactase, that undigested lactose travels straight to your colon, where gut bacteria ferment it and produce the gas, cramping, and diarrhea.

5
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:48,560
Three changes make the biggest difference: the type of dairy you choose, how you eat it, and replacing the enzyme you're missing.

6
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:50,640
First, the type of dairy matters.

7
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:53,600
Fresh milk keeps its lactose fully intact.

8
00:00:53,920 --> 00:01:04,960
But hard, aged cheeses like cheddar, parmesan, gouda, and gruyere test at under a tenth of a gram of lactose per serving, because the bacteria used in aging consume it over time.

9
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:08,960
Reach for Greek yogurt or an aged cheese before regular milk.

10
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:12,160
Second, how you eat it changes everything.

11
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:19,120
Your body can only break down so much lactose at once, so a full glass on an empty stomach overwhelms it fast.

12
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:26,000
Spread your dairy across the day instead of one big serving, pair it with other food, and skip drinking it on an empty stomach.

13
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:28,880
Third, replace the missing enzyme.

14
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:33,120
Lactase supplements work by supplying the enzyme your gut isn't making enough of.

15
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:40,880
Take one to three caplets right with your first bite of dairy, and each dose covers roughly thirty to forty-five minutes of eating.

16
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:47,120
Switching up the type of dairy you eat and how you eat it makes lactose intolerance a lot easier to live with.

17
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:56,560
But if you're losing weight without trying or seeing blood in your stool, that points to something beyond lactose intolerance — see a doctor to find the real cause.
